cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Open Global Liquidity in research, please cite this software and identify the data
  vintage or snapshot generation time used in your analysis.
title: "Open Global Liquidity"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sampaio"
    given-names: "Yuri"
    email: "ysmp@proton.me"
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-09-03
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/y-sam/open-global-liquidity"
url: "https://open-global-liquidity.streamlit.app/"
abstract: >-
  Transparent, reproducible public-data research infrastructure for experimental US liquidity
  models, a five-central-bank USD-normalized global balance-sheet momentum model, and separate
  collateral, offshore-dollar-credit, and US private-liquidity research layers. The project is
  independent and does not reproduce or claim access to CrossBorder Capital's proprietary
  methodology, data, or models.
keywords:
  - global liquidity
  - monetary liquidity
  - quantitative macroeconomics
  - Bitcoin
  - reproducible research
